{
  "name": "Create fluidX THE EYE live camera sessions with SMS/email invites, AI analysis, and Google Drive",
  "nodes": [
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "### Setup \u2014 Create a fluidX revXR THE EYE session\n\n**Goal:** Invite the customer (SMS and/or email) and notify the service agent via email so all join the fluidX THE EYE session and share their cameras live.\n\n**Form fields:**\n- `Agent Email Address` \u2014 required, always sent.\n- `User Phone Number` \u2014 optional. If filled, an SMS with the join link is sent.\n- `User Email Address` \u2014 optional. If filled, an email with the join link is sent.\n- Empty user fields are skipped (IF nodes gate each branch).\n\n1. Sign in at https://live.fluidx.digital (activate the TEST ABO plan, \u20ac0) and create your API key.\n2. Review the API docs: https://live.fluidx.digital/api/swagger.html.\n3. In n8n add credentials:\n   - fluidX API key (HTTP Header Auth \u2192 header x-api-key)\n   - SMTP account for outbound email (used for both Agent and User emails).\n   - OpenAI key\n   - Google Drive API\n4. Open the \"Set Config\" node \u2014 the defaults are ready to test; adjust other values if needed (the form collects phone/email each run).\n5. Run the flow: Submit the form \u2192 Create Session \u2192 Set Session Vars \u2192 Create Drive folder \u2192 If Phone Set? \u2192 (SMS) \u2192 If User Email Set? \u2192 (User Email) \u2192 Agent Email \u2192 Wait \u2192 Poll \u2192 Drive uploads.\n6. Create a THEEYE folder in your Google Drive root.\n\nTips:\n- Keep secrets inside n8n credentials or environment variables.\n- Use demo data while testing; swap to production values when ready.\n- Log out of live.fluidx.digital in the agent's browser before testing to ensure the invite flow opens a clean session.\n",
        "height": 540,
        "width": 688
      },
      "id": "0d2978ac-0459-47fd-9b99-9851852cad04",
      "name": "\ud83d\udcdd Setup & Instructions",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        0,
